        <body>
            <div xml:id="d757">

                <pb facs="0869" n="749" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg749"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador McCormick to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-02-06"><hi rendition="#italic">February 6,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 211.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my cablegram of January 7 and
                    to those of Mr. Eddy dated, respectively, January 3 and 6, in which it was
                    requested that the owners of the cargo shipped on board the steamship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Arabia</hi> should, with as little delay as possible,
                    forward to this embassy full proof of their inability to communicate directly
                    with Vladivostok, together with their affidavits to that effect, I have now the
                    honor to inform you that, up to this day, I have received none of these
                    documents, nor has Mr. Berline, counselor of the embassy, had any word from the
                    owners on this subject.</p>
                <p>I therefore beg to suggest that the attention of the owners may be called to the
                    fact that since they have not seen fit to comply with this very reasonable
                    requirement of the admiralty court neither the State Department, this embassy,
                    nor Mr. Berline can be held responsible in case it should prove impossible to
                    obtain a rehearing of the case.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert S.
                    McCormick.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
